  "summary": "The health-tech landscape shows major momentum in three key areas: pharmaceutical benefit managers face new regulatory pressure with proposed transparency rules attracting significant attention across coverage, while Anthropic's AI platform Claude Science is gaining traction in drug development with backing from major players like Evernorth's $100 million specialty pharmacy investment. Healthcare organizations are increasingly deploying AI for clinical and operational tasks—from EMR-based algorithms identifying cancer therapy risks to workforce planning and documentation tools—though executives are being cautious about implementation and governance remains a collaborative challenge. Notable regulatory approvals include Orca Bio's T-cell therapy for blood cancer patients and Aurenar's breakthrough designation for a brain-bleed device, while emerging research explores synthetic biology and pandemic-preparedness diagnostics alongside growing evidence that GLP-1 drugs may benefit peripheral artery disease patients.",
